1	//! Free-running per-rank engines. Every logical DP rank is an autonomous
2	//! engine: its own request queue, slots, KV pool, offload/P-D state, and
3	//! load feed, driven by its own thread. There is no coordinator — the only
4	//! coupling between engines is the fixed-cadence DeepEP collective chain
5	//! itself (75 MoE layers per step plus the fixed MTP round): every engine
6	//! steps unconditionally, idle ranks enter with padding rows, and the
7	//! collective's back-pressure is the synchronization. The invariants that
8	//! make that safe are structural, not negotiated: a fixed chain (no
9	//! conditional collectives), conservative protocol-max shapes, and
10	//! deterministic padding rows (`docs/models/glm52/free-running-dp.md` §4).
11	//!
12	//! Each engine admits up to `GLM52_MAX_BATCH_PER_RANK` requests from its own
13	//! queue (the `EngineHandle` routes frontend requests to rank queues by
14	//! `data_parallel_rank`). KV pages come from the rank's [`BlockPool`]
15	//! (64-token pages, content-hashed blocks): admission reserves a request's
16	//! full-lifetime page count up front (honor-or-reject — a request that can
17	//! never fit is rejected, one that can't fit *now* stays queued), so decode
18	//! can never run out of pages mid-request, and released requests' sealed
19	//! blocks stay matchable as the prefix cache.
20	//!
21	//! Every step the engine forwards its OWN batch bucket — each active slot's
22	//! *span* of next tokens (mid-prefill slots batch up to a bucket of
23	//! consecutive prompt positions through one step; decode slots feed one
24	//! row), idle slots feed a padding row whose output is discarded. The
25	//! bucket is the smallest member of `GLM52_DECODE_BUCKETS` covering the
26	//! rank's own row demand. The TP4 replicated topology is the N=1
27	//! special case: ONE logical rank's engine drives every mirrored worker
28	//! with the identical step, and the join asserts bit-identical results (the
29	//! replicated-activations contract); as the sole issuer of its collectives
30	//! it may block while fully idle instead of free-running.
31	//!
32	//! The per-request decisions (what to feed next, what a step's output means)
33	//! live in [`Glm52SlotState`] as pure data transitions, and the
34	//! admission/step-shape decisions in [`admission`] / [`plan`] as pure
35	//! functions over the occupancy and feed wants.
36	
